  "key_findings": "1. Tool Wear is the ONLY sensor with a statistically significant difference between residual failures and normal machines (dev: p = 1.22e-17, full: p = 1.61e-23). The median tool wear for residual failures is ~210 min (IQR: 17 min) vs 107 min for normals (IQR: 108 min). 2. All other operational sensors \u2014 Torque (p = 0.39), Rotational Speed (p = 0.87), Air Temp (p = 0.19), and Process Temp (p = 0.43) \u2014 have identical distributions between residual failures and normal machines with p > 0.10. 3. Residual failures consist almost entirely of Tool Wear Failures (TWF, 34 in dev, 43 in full) and unlabelled anomalies (7 in dev, 9 in full). Because TWF occurs stochastically between 200 and 240 mins without physical sensor anomalies, machine learning models cannot separate them without triggering unacceptable false alarms."
}